3. Infrastructure & Scalability Strategy

Current Approach
The current infrastructure strategy is intentionally lean during the validation stage to avoid premature infrastructure scaling before workflow and product validation are completed.
Current infrastructure priorities:
Validate operational scalability
Stress-test critical database workflows
Optimize real-time chat performance
Stabilize frontend responsiveness
Improve operational reliability under load
Supabase is currently being used as the primary backend environment to validate:
Database scalability
Query performance
Real-time event handling
Operational throughput
Infrastructure stability under stress conditions
Long-Term Infrastructure Direction
AWS migration is planned as a later-stage infrastructure evolution after:
Product stabilization
Workflow validation
Controlled rollout completion
Early operational scale confirmation
Current assessment is that immediate infrastructure migration before validation would introduce unnecessary operational complexity during the learning phase.
Enterprise Infrastructure & Compliance Roadmap
Post-Phase 2 priorities include:
Enterprise API readiness
Infrastructure hardening
Security compliance readiness
SOC2 evaluation
Enterprise integration support
Scalable API monetization opportunities

4. Legal, Compliance & Governance Dependencies

PULSE's rollout strategy is being executed alongside a parallel legal, compliance, and governance review process to ensure operational expansion, enterprise onboarding, and commercial scaling remain aligned with regulatory and organizational requirements.
The current validation phase is intentionally structured to allow operational learning and infrastructure stabilization prior to broader enterprise dependency or commercial-scale rollout.
Current Legal & Governance Focus Areas
Entity and operational structure review
FEMA and regulatory assessment
Commercial framework documentation
Platform terms and policy development
Data protection and platform governance review
Enterprise onboarding and liability assessment
Risk and compliance evaluation for scale readiness
Current Status
Legal and compliance workstreams remain active and are treated as a mandatory governance layer prior to broader enterprise rollout or commercial scaling.
Operational validation activities are therefore being conducted within a controlled soft-launch environment pending completion of:
Regulatory review
Commercial governance alignment
Compliance assessment
Enterprise-readiness approvals

