6. Readiness Gate Framework

Phase 0 → Phase 1 (Enterprise Pilot Readiness)
Required Conditions:
Stable trip workflow under internal testing
Minimum 60% trip completion consistency
Driver app operational stability
Database stress validation completed
No unresolved critical workflow failures
Initial legal and compliance review completed
Progression Approval:
Product Lead
Operations Review
Leadership alignment
Escalation / Pause Conditions:
Trip completion below 50% for two consecutive weeks
Critical workflow instability
Infrastructure instability under load
Regulatory or governance risks identified during review
Phase 1 → Phase 2 (TMS Transition Readiness)
Required Conditions:
25–40 active supplier organizations
Repeat monthly operational usage established
Stable ledger workflow usage
Infrastructure scalability confidence established
Enterprise operational dependency validated
Commercial and enterprise governance framework validated
Progression Approval:
Product Lead
Operational Review
Leadership approval
Escalation / Pause Conditions:
High operational support dependency
Enterprise workflow failures
Supplier adoption instability
Infrastructure reliability concerns
Phase 2 → Phase 3 (Expansion Readiness)
Required Conditions:
Stable operational throughput
Repeat organizational usage established
Integrated trip adoption validated
Infrastructure migration readiness confirmed
Legal, regulatory, and commercial scalability review completed
Progression Approval:
Leadership review
Operational sign-off
Commercial alignment
Escalation / Pause Conditions:
Infrastructure instability
Workflow failure at scale
Commercial or governance limitations
Low repeat engagement

